# Title: Sensitive File Recovery From Backup Via Wbadmin.EXE
# ID: 84972c80-251c-4c3a-9079-4f00aad93938
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), frack113
# Date: 2024-05-10
# Tags: attack.credential-access, attack.t1003.003
# Description: Detects the dump of highly sensitive files such as "NTDS.DIT" and "SECURITY" hive.
# Attackers can leverage the "wbadmin" utility in order to dump sensitive files that might contain credential or sensitive information.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((process.command_line:* recovery* AND process.command_line:*recoveryTarget* AND process.command_line:*itemtype:File*) AND (process.command_line:*\\config\\SAM* OR process.command_line:*\\config\\SECURITY* OR process.command_line:*\\config\\SYSTEM* OR process.command_line:*\\Windows\\NTDS\\NTDS.dit*)) AND ((process.executable:*\\wbadmin.exe) OR (process.pe.original_file_name:"WBADMIN.EXE")))
